    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-civil-engeering-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Civil Engeering 495991 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Nov 15 2026 Position Description Shape the future of sustainable infrastructure through industry-connected teaching and research. Build your academic career with opportunities for research funding, HDR supervision and industry collaboration. Based in Townsville where you can enjoy a tropical lifestyle, with affordable living and the Great Barrier Reef on your doorstep. Full time (36.25 hours per week) | Continuing Appointment Academic Level B - $112,810 - $133,110 Academic Level C - $137,166 - $157,465 Plus 17% super and excellent benefits incl. 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading and flexible work arrangements Shape the future of sustainable infrastructure in the tropics At James Cook University (JCU), our location drives our purpose. Positioned in the heart of Northern Australia, we tackle some of the world's most pressing environmental, infrastructure and sustainability challenges. We're seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Civil Engineering to help shape the next generation of engineers and deliver research that creates real impact across tropical and regional communities. This is a unique opportunity to join a growing Civil Engineering discipline and build your academic career in a region where your expertise can directly influence industry, government and community outcomes. About the Opportunity As a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, you will strengthen JCU's teaching, research and industry engagement in Civil Engineering, with expertise in Geotechnical Engineering and/or related disciplines. You will contribute to a sustainable future through high-quality teaching, impactful research and meaningful collaboration with industry and government partners. You'll have the opportunity to: Deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Civil Engineering and related disciplines. Develop and lead a research program addressing challenges relevant to Northern Australia and the tropics. Secure research and consulting income through industry, government and competitive funding opportunities. Supervise Honours, Masters and Higher Degree Research students. Collaborate with industry partners across sectors including mining, critical minerals, sustainable infrastructure and emerging technologies. Raise the profile and impact of JCU's Civil Engineering discipline through research excellence, partnerships and community engagement. About You You are an emerging or established academic who is passionate about engineering education and creating research impact. You will bring: A PhD in Civil Engineering or a closely related discipline. Expertise in Geotechnical Engineering or related areas such as soil mechanics, rock mechanics, mining or sustainable infrastructure. A proven or emerging research profile, demonstrated through publications and research activity. Experience, or strong potential, to attract research funding and build industry partnerships. A commitment to high-quality teaching and student success. The ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and engage effectively with industry, government and community stakeholders. Why JCU? At JCU, your work matters. You'll be part of a university internationally recognised for its focus on the tropics and commitment to creating positive change through education and research. We offer: A supportive and collaborative academic environment. Opportunities to build industry-connected research programs. Access to world-class research facilities and partnerships. Generous leave provisions and flexible work practices. A vibrant tropical lifestyle in Townsville, with easy access to the Great Barrier Reef, rainforests and outdoor adventures. Why Townsville? Enjoy the best of career and lifestyle in Townsville. As Northern Australia's largest city, Townsville offers a thriving engineering sector, affordable living, a vibrant coastal community, and more than 300 days of sunshine each year. With the Great Barrier Reef, Magnetic Island and tropical rainforests on your doorstep, it's the perfect place to build an impactful career while enjoying an exceptional work-life balance. Ready to Make an Impact? If you're excited by the opportunity to influence the future of Civil Engineering education and research while contributing to sustainable outcomes for Northern Australia and the tropical world, we'd love to hear from you. Click the ‘apply’ button where you will be asked to complete an application form or alternatively, please apply directly via the via the JCU careers page and follow the below steps: Complete the application form Upload your current resume Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Mahmood Sadat Noori (07) 4781 5769 or via email Mahmood.SadatNoori@jcu.edu.au Apply now and help build resilient infrastructure and communities for the future. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/space-systems-coordinator-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Space Systems Coordinator",
      "description": "Space Systems Coordinator - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Space Systems Coordinator 495841 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an organised, analytical and customer-focused professional who enjoys turning complex information into practical outcomes? Join James Cook University as our Space Systems Coordinator and help strengthen the quality, accessibility and use of space and building information across the University. We now have an exciting opportunity for a skilled Space Systems Coordinator to join the Estate Directorate within the Services Division. Full-time opportunity | 36.25 hours per week | Full-time role. Townsville location | Travel between campuses may be required from time to time. HEWL 6: $90,821 - $98,369 plus up to 17% superannuation. ABOUT THE ROLE As Space Systems Coordinator, you will maintain accurate and accessible space, building and occupancy information across JCU's facilities and space management systems. You will coordinate data validation, system updates, desktop and on-site audits, and prepare reliable plans, reports and analysis to inform space allocation, utilisation, workplace planning and minor works decisions. Working closely with University stakeholders, you will provide responsive systems support, training and guidance, resolve complex data and workflow issues, coordinate requests and inspections, and identify practical improvements to systems, data and service processes. You will also help ensure records and activities meet relevant University requirements, building information standards and workplace health and safety obligations. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring relevant qualifications and experience, together with demonstrated experience administering information, facilities, space management or comparable corporate systems. You will be confident maintaining data integrity, resolving complex system and data issues, and using sound judgement to manage competing priorities under general to broad direction. Strong analytical, problem-solving, written communication, consultation and customer service skills are essential, including the ability to prepare clear reports and guidance, deliver training and build productive relationships across organisational levels. Knowledge of data governance, records management and facilities compliance, and experience with CAD, GIS, building information modelling or space visualisation tools, will be highly regarded. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper. 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading. 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year. Up to 6 months paid parental leave. A range of flexible working options. Staff study assistance and paid study leave. Ongoing professional development support. Fitness Passport. Corporate discount on health insurance. Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling). Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses. HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Nathan Shepherd, Associate Director Planning and Capital Development at nathan.shepherd@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    }
